# libubootenv configuration for the Mender + barebox demo.
#
# A single, non-redundant U-Boot-format environment living raw in its own GPT
# partition (partlabel mender-bootenv). The same partition is described to
# barebox by the barebox,uboot-environment device-tree node (device-path) added
# in meta-mender-barebox/recipes-bsp/barebox/files/dts, so fw_setenv/fw_printenv
# from userspace and barebox' ubootvar driver read and write the exact same
# bytes.
#
# Format note: the partition holds a bare mkenvimage output -- a 4-byte CRC32
# followed by NUL-separated KEY=VALUE pairs -- which is what both libubootenv
# (non-redundant) and barebox' ubootvar driver expect. barebox' ubootvar CRCs
# the ENTIRE partition cdev, so the env size MUST equal the partition size;
# keep the mkenvimage size, the size here, and the wks partition size all equal
# (1 MiB).
#
# @ENV_DEVICE@ is substituted per machine by the recipe from
# BAREBOX_MENDER_ENV_DEVICE (e.g. /dev/mmcblk0p2 on RPi4, /dev/vda2 on qemu).
#
# Device          Offset   Env. size
@ENV_DEVICE@      0x0000   0x100000
